---
/**
 * Prove the problem is real using somebody else's reporting, in the fewest
 * possible words, attributed and linked.
 *
 * Placement is deliberate: not the opener (as an opener this is a grievance) and
 * not a footnote (as a footnote it is wasted). It sits between the appetite and
 * the door, explaining a restriction the reader has just been given a reason to
 * care about.
 *
 * Every number here was verified against the article before it shipped, and we
 * never name the chains in our own copy — the link does that.
 */
import { CBC } from '../lib/claims';
---
<section class="section section--tight why">
  <div class="container">
    <hr class="rule" />
    <div class="why-body">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Why the list is short</p>

      <p class="body why-para" data-reveal>
        In October 2024, CBC Marketplace sent an undercover team into {CBC.locations} Greater
        Toronto Area locations of five well-known chains. Employees at {CBC.claimedCertified} of
        them said the whole restaurant was halal-certified. <strong>Not one of the ten was.</strong>
      </p>

      <p class="body why-para" data-reveal>
        In those six visits, staff produced a certificate belonging to their <em>meat supplier</em> —
        a real document, certifying the meat — and used it to suggest the kitchen itself was
        certified. The team was also shown {CBC.expiredShown} expired certificates. One had run
        out eight years earlier.
      </p>

      <p class="body why-para" data-reveal>
        Nobody in that story is lying on purpose. The system is confusing, and the person who
        carries the doubt home is you. Those two failures — a supplier's certificate standing in
        for a kitchen's, and a certificate that quietly ran out — are checks six and five below.
      </p>

      <p class="mono why-src" data-reveal>
        Source: CBC Marketplace, {CBC.date} —
        <a href={CBC.url} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">read the investigation →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <hr class="rule" />
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Cream, not a dark band. The dark budget is spent on the refusal and the
     footer; spending a third on a grievance would make the page feel aggrieved. */
  .why { background: var(--surface-base); }
  .why-body { padding-block: 44px; max-width: 640px; }
  .why-para { margin-bottom: 18px; font-size: var(--t-lede); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .why-para:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 26px; }
  .why-para strong { font-weight: 800; }
  .why-para em { font-style: italic; }

  /* The only non-orange link on the page: attribution is not a call to action. */
  .why-src a {
    color: var(--text-primary);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }

  @media (max-width: 639px) {
    .why-body { padding-block: 30px; }
    .why-para { margin-bottom: 14px; }
    .why-para:last-of-type { margin-bottom: 20px; }
  }
</style>
